diff --git a/ONYX_BRINGUP.md b/ONYX_BRINGUP.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a5d1ecb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ONYX_BRINGUP.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Onyx XNU 12377 source checkpoint
+
+This tree is not a bootable iOS 26 image. Base XNU is
+ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f. Generic UniXNU build prerequisites
+were applied in commit 817b59d. The BCM2837 machine configuration is used as
+the generic ARM64 build target, not as Raspberry Pi hardware support.
+
+The Onyx-specific change wires pe_init_fiq to the existing working Group 1
+GICv3 path instead of Apple's default Group 0 FIQ setup. The build target is
+restricted to one CPU and one cluster. PSCI secondary startup is intentionally
+not provided; an unexpected stop SGI fails explicitly. The two early register
+waits are bounded by the architected counter, without requiring timer IRQs.
+The DT GIC windows must exactly match the known Onyx loader before any mapping:
+physical distributor 0x17100000/0x10000, redistributors 0x17180000/0x100000,
+SoC window base 0x00400000. No memory or MMIO address is borrowed from SM8550.
+
+bsd/dev/onyx_ufshc.c is the staged native transport from the working Onyx tree,
+updated to consume XNU 12377 machine/pmap/cache prototypes and vm_kern_xnu.h
+for contiguous buffer allocation. It is NOT in the BSD source list yet. It
+still requires the RDWBLOCK loader-page adapter, logging hook, sysctl parent,
+GPT/block-device registration and quiesce integration. No storage initialization
+or write path is invoked by this checkpoint. The internal journal policy is
+preserved byte-for-byte; the imported driver is not a writable installer.
+
+Run: sh onyx-tests/run.sh
+
+Observed host results: GIC affinity packing and counter wrap/deadlines;
+Group 1 timer routing, timer dispatch/EOI, masking an unknown SPI;
+malformed DT size/layout refusal before mapping; CPU gate; redistributor and
+RWP timeout; exact journal range, CRC and 288 command mutations. The GIC test
+uses fake MMIO and kernel API shims. It is not a kernel ABI build or hardware
+qualification. No first-boot kernel is linked here.
+
+Before hardware use: complete the non-Apple startup/CPU/pmap platform patches,
+prepare the matching compiler/KDK/SDK/dependency archives, compile/link this
+kernel against actual XNU headers, audit the ARM64e fixup/entry contract, and
+wire the loader-compatible framebuffer/console and panic capture. After a
+console/timer checkpoint, enable the storage adapter and read-only root path.
+The 16.5 kernel's APFS and userland shims cannot be assumed compatible with 26.
